From nobody Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: moleksy <moleksy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 14:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net/iavf: skip IPsec TX callbacks without security offload

iavf_xmit_pkts() always hands ci_xmit_pkts() its IPsec ops, so every
packet makes a get_ipsec_desc() call and every segment a
calc_segment_len() call, also on a queue without
RTE_ETH_TX_OFFLOAD_SECURITY.

Pass the ops only when the queue has the offload, as ixgbe already
gates its IPsec path on the queue. For a packet without
RTE_MBUF_F_TX_SEC_OFFLOAD the descriptors and segment lengths are
unchanged: get_ipsec_desc() adds no descriptor and calc_segment_len()
returns data_len, which is what ci_xmit_pkts() uses for NULL ops. A
packet that sets the flag on a queue without the offload breaks the
ethdev contract, which lists the offload as used by the flag, and now
leaves without an IPsec descriptor.

On an E810 VF with 2-segment ST 2110-20 packets one scheduler core went
from 7.38 to 7.53 Mpps (core capped at 2.0 GHz).

MTL: drop once upstream DPDK gates the iavf IPsec ops on the offload.

Signed-off-by: moleksy <moleksy@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/net/intel/iavf/iavf_rxtx.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/intel/iavf/iavf_rxtx.c b/drivers/net/intel/iavf/iavf_rxtx.c
--- a/drivers/net/intel/iavf/iavf_rxtx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/intel/iavf/iavf_rxtx.c
@@ -2605,7 +2605,9 @@
 	return ci_xmit_pkts(txq, tx_pkts, nb_pkts,
 			    (txq->vlan_flag & IAVF_TX_FLAGS_VLAN_TAG_LOC_L2TAG1) ?
 				CI_VLAN_IN_L2TAG1 : CI_VLAN_IN_L2TAG2,
-			    iavf_get_context_desc, &ipsec_ops, NULL);
+			    iavf_get_context_desc,
+			    (txq->offloads & RTE_ETH_TX_OFFLOAD_SECURITY) ? &ipsec_ops : NULL,
+			    NULL);
 }
 
